{"id":"h286","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Danube flows into the Black Sea.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Danube flows into the Black Sea through its delta in Romania and Ukraine.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Danube is a major European river rising in the Black Forest region of Germany.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Danube flows about 2,850 km southeast through ten countries.","confidence":0.85,"lean":1,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The Danube's mouth is at the Black Sea, where it splits into the Sulina, Sfântu Gheorghe, and Chilia branches forming the delta.","confidence":0.93,"lean":1,"theta":1.4608,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The river does not empty directly into the Black Sea at a single point but spreads across a delta and branches.","confidence":0.85,"lean":-0.2,"theta":1.3352,"phi":0.0},{"text":"A loose reading might suggest the river ends in a lagoon or lake system rather than the sea.","confidence":0.2,"lean":-0.4,"theta":0.3142,"phi":-3.1416},{"text":"The delta's channels do reach the sea.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Some might confuse the Danube with rivers that flow into the Aegean or Mediterranean, but that does not apply.","confidence":0.1,"lean":-0.3,"theta":0.1571,"phi":3.1416},{"text":"It is well established that the Danube's delta channels discharge into the Black Sea.","confidence":0.97,"lean":1,"theta":1.5237,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The delta's complexity does not change the fact that the river ends in the Black Sea.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":4,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":5,"J":-0.4,"relation":"contradicts"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"